* FRI\ntwelve cards
** Objects
*** Low-degree polynomial\n//few coefficients, many evaluations//
*** Reed-Solomon code\n//polynomial → evaluations; different polynomials rarely agree//
*** Rate\n//rho = d/n; work below 1 - sqrt(rho)//
** The property
*** Proximity\n//close to a polynomial, not necessarily equal to one//
*** IOP of proximity\n//accept codewords, reject the far, read few entries//
left side
** Commitments and challenges
*** Merkle commitment\n//root = the whole table; path = one entry//
*** Random challenge\n//r after the commitment, never before//
*** Folding\n//combine f(x) and f(-x); halve the degree//
** The protocol
*** Commit phase\n//commit → challenge → fold, repeat until tiny//
*** Final polynomial\n//the last layer is sent in the clear//
*** Query phase\n//one position, checked through every layer, repeated//
*** FRI\n//fold it down, then spot-check every layer//
@endmindmap
